
== §1 — SPEC INTEGRITY AND NO-DRIFT ==
  ✓ browser spec is byte-identical to acs_coord.json
  ✓ schema and detector version are pinned
  ✓ severities are INFO/WARNING/ERROR only — no UNSAFE, no FATAL, no VIOLATION
  ✓ every clash type has a declared severity
  ✓ an unknown clash type never silently becomes an ERROR
  ✓ RESOLVED is not an automatic status
  ✓ only cross-discipline pairs are declared
  ✓ the spec names no code, standard or authority
  ✓ no auto-fix vocabulary is offered as an outcome

== §2 — TEST A: SERVICE THROUGH STRUCTURE ==
  ✓ a duct crossing a beam is reported as a HARD_CLASH
  ✓ the clash pairs MEP with STRUCTURE
  ✓ the clash carries a positive intersection volume
  ✓ the clash carries both world AABBs as evidence
  ✓ a clash from stated dimensions is labelled stated
  ✓ the clash id is deterministic across two runs
  ✓ the clash never claims the duct was moved or the beam resized

== §3 — TEST B/C: PENETRATIONS ==
  ✓ a pipe crossing a wall with no penetration reports OPENING_REQUIRED
  ✓ OPENING_REQUIRED is a finding, never an instruction
  ✓ no opening was actually created in the model
  ✓ a declared penetration that covers the crossing suppresses the finding
  ✓ the suppression is recorded, never silent
  ✓ the suppression names both elements and the penetration
  ✓ a penetration that does not cover the crossing reports PENETRATION_UNRESOLVED
  ✓ a represented penetration never claims approval or firestopping
  ✓ no sleeve size is ever produced

== §4 — TEST D/E: HOSTS AND DUPLICATES ==
  ✓ a column standing in a declared door opening is reported
  ✓ the same column is also reported against the host wall
  ✓ nothing claims the door is blocked, unsafe or non-compliant
  ✓ two FLS devices sharing one source element report DUPLICATE_OCCUPANCY
  ✓ DUPLICATE_OCCUPANCY is INFO, never an error
  ✓ an FLS device never clashes with the MEP element it references

== §5 — TEST F: WORLD COORDINATES, NOT LOCAL ==
  ✓ a rotated building finds the same conflicts
  ✓ a translated and rotated building finds the same conflicts
  ✓ rotation actually moved the geometry (no world-axis shortcut)
  ✓ rotated coordinates stay finite and quantised
  ✓ a rotated box uses the separating-axis test, not its AABB

== §6 — TEST G: PROJECT SCOPE ==
  ✓ two distant buildings produce no cross-building clash
  ✓ two overlapping buildings do produce cross-building clashes
  ✓ every clash names the building of each side
  ✓ two buildings with identical local coordinates are not merged
  ✓ placement is part of the snapshot identity
  ✓ a project snapshot has no single revision hash
  ✓ a project snapshot still has a deterministic project hash

== §7 — TEST H: SNAPSHOT INTEGRITY AND RECONCILIATION ==
  ✓ an unchanged model reports CURRENT
  ✓ a changed model reports STALE_MODEL_CHANGED, never a silent re-run
  ✓ a stale snapshot is never presented as current
  ✓ a snapshot with no hash is UNVERIFIABLE, never assumed current
  ✓ a clash whose geometry vanished is RESOLVED_BY_MODEL_CHANGE
  ✓ reconciliation never claims the change was correct
  ✓ a clash present in both snapshots is PERSISTING
  ✓ a clash appearing only in the newer snapshot is NEW
  ✓ an acknowledged clash that disappears becomes OBSOLETE, not resolved
  ✓ reconciliation states are exactly the declared four

== §8 — TEST I: SEMANTIC AND REFERENCE INTEGRITY ==
  ✓ a dangling cross-discipline reference is reported
  ✓ an unresolved penetration host is a semantic conflict
  ✓ reference findings are ERROR severity
  ✓ a reference finding carries the reporting discipline and its source code
  ✓ reference findings are re-classified, never invented here
  ✓ a reference finding is not dressed as a safety judgement

== §9 — EXEMPTIONS ARE SEMANTIC, NEVER TYPE-BLIND ==
  ✓ every applied exemption is a declared kind
  ✓ a column crossing the slab of its own levels is exempt
  ✓ a column crossing a slab outside its own levels is NOT exempt
  ✓ an opening is exempt only inside its declared host wall
  ✓ a declared void or core has no matter to collide with
  ✓ a void suppression is recorded on the pair it suppressed
  ✓ no exemption is granted on element kind alone

== §10 — CLEARANCE ONLY WHERE STATED ==
  ✓ a stated clearance produces a CLEARANCE_CLASH
  ✓ the clash carries the stated clearance and nothing invented
  ✓ CLEARANCE_CLASH is INFO, never an error
  ✓ no clearance is invented where none is stated
  ✓ a stated clearance widens the broad phase so the pair is not missed
  ✓ no maintenance, service or code clearance appears anywhere

== §11 — NO AUTO-FIX, NO REDESIGN, NO MUTATION ==
  ✓ no snapshot contains an auto-fix, reroute or resize claim
  ✓ no snapshot claims compliance, safety or adequacy
  ✓ every snapshot declares compliance NOT_EVALUATED
  ✓ the detector mutates no source model
  ✓ the detector mutates no compiled discipline model
  ✓ a status change is only ever an explicit human decision
  ✓ an accepted decision records who decided and on what basis
  ✓ a status change on an unknown clash is refused

== §12 — NAVIGATION AND EGRESS ARE UNTOUCHED ==
  ✓ the spec states coordination does not affect navigation
  ✓ no snapshot emits a route, path or reroute
  ✓ a column blocking a door does not alter the door relationship

== §13 — EVIDENCE AND GEOMETRY CONFIDENCE ==
  ✓ every geometric clash carries an intersection with positive volume
  ✓ every clash carries the detector version
  ✓ every geometric clash declares its geometry confidence
  ✓ a fallback-sized clash names which side fell back
  ✓ a display fallback is never promoted to a stated dimension
  ✓ proximity alone never produces a hard clash
  ✓ a shared face is contact, not intersection

== §14 — BROAD PHASE AND SCALE ==
  ✓ an empty model yields no pairs and no cells
  ✓ the grid cell size comes from the spec, not from code
  ✓ same-discipline pairs are never candidates
  ✓ cross-discipline pairs sharing a cell are candidates
  ✓ an oversized element is still compared against everything
  ✓ the statistics report the real candidate-pair count, never a rounded claim
  ✓ the busiest cell occupancy is reported rather than hidden

== §15 — DEBUG VIEW AND EXPORT ==
  ✓ the debug view highlights exactly the two elements
  ✓ the debug view provides an intersection marker box
  ✓ the debug view states it changes nothing in the normal model
  ✓ an unknown clash has no debug view
  ✓ the export is marked derived
  ✓ the export says it is never persisted as model truth
  ✓ the export carries the snapshot and model hashes
  ✓ the export carries every clash with its evidence

== §16 — RULE INPUTS ARE FACTS, NOT RULES ==
  ✓ rule inputs are counts and existence flags only
  ✓ every declared rule input family is present
  ✓ a count is never compared to a threshold
  ✓ a model with no clashes reports zero, not missing
  ✓ every clash type has a count, including the zero ones

== §17 — EMPTY AND DEGENERATE MODELS ==
  ✓ a model with no structure, MEP or fire data still compiles
  ✓ an empty model is not reported as coordinated or clear
  ✓ a model with MEP but no structure produces no structural clash
  ✓ the broken MEP fixture still yields a snapshot, not a crash
  ✓ a model with no MEP at all yields no MEP clash

== §18 — SORTING, IDS AND DETERMINISM ==
  ✓ the clash id is a sha256-derived deterministic token
  ✓ the same conflict in the same elements always has the same id
  ✓ a different conflict type produces a different id
  ✓ clash ids are unique inside a snapshot
  ✓ clashes are sorted deterministically by severity then type then element
  ✓ two runs of the whole fixture set are byte-identical

== §19 — FILTERS AND LOOKUP ==
  ✓ filtering by discipline pair returns only that pair
  ✓ filtering by severity returns only that severity
  ✓ filtering by an unknown building returns nothing
  ✓ filtering by the real building returns everything
  ✓ lookup by id returns the clash and nothing for an unknown id

== §20 — SUMMARY HONESTY ==
  ✓ the summary never claims the model is coordinated or clear
  ✓ the summary states detection and traceability only
  ✓ the summary counts match the clash list
  ✓ the summary reports exemptions rather than hiding them
  ✓ the summary reports geometry confidence

